      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Find the cofactor of ${p}_{35}$ in \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & \\sqrt{13} & 0 & 1 \\\\ -25 & -1 & -5 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 3 & \\sqrt{2} & -9 & 7\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "First, to get the minor of ${p}_{35}$, we remove the $3$rd row and $5$th column: \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 & 2 & 1 & ∗ \\\\ 3 & 5 & \\sqrt{13} & 0 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 3 & 8 & ∗ \\\\ 11 & 3 & \\sqrt{2} & -9 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{35}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & \\sqrt{13} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 11 & 3 & \\sqrt{2} & -9\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of ${p}_{35}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{35} & =(-1)^{3+5}{M}_{35} \\\\  & ={M}_{35} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & \\sqrt{13} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 11 & 3 & \\sqrt{2} & -9\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
